.TH "GLANCES" "1" "Oct 11, 2026" "5.0.0b1" "Glances"
.SH NAME
glances \- An eye on your system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.sp
\fBglances\fP [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.sp
\fBglances\fP is a cross\-platform curses\-based monitoring tool that aims
to present a maximum of information in a minimum of space, ideally fitting
in a classic 80x24 terminal or larger for more details. It can adapt
dynamically to the displayed information depending on the terminal size.
It can also work in client/server mode.
Remote monitoring can be performed via a terminal, a web interface or
the RESTful API (served by the FastAPI based server mode).
.sp
\fBglances\fP is written in Python and uses the \fIpsutil\fP library to get
information from your system.
.SH OPTIONS
.SH COMMAND-LINE OPTIONS
.SS General
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show this help message and exit
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
show the program’s version number and exit
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-debug
enable debug\-level logging
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-print\-completion {bash,zsh,tcsh,fish,powershell}
print the shell tab completion script for the Glances CLI (not available
on Windows)
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-C <path>, \-\-config <path>
path to the \fBglances.conf\fP file to use (instead of searching
\fB~/.config/glances/glances.conf\fP, then \fB/etc/glances/glances.conf\fP)
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-modules\-list, \-\-module\-list
print the plugins and exporters lists and exit
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-disable\-plugin <a,b>, \-\-disable\-plugins <a,b>, \-\-disable <a,b>
disable plugins (comma\-separated list or \fBall\fP). If \fBall\fP is used,
then you need to configure \fB\-\-enable\-plugin\fP
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-enable\-plugin <a,b>, \-\-enable\-plugins <a,b>, \-\-enable <a,b>
enable plugins (comma\-separated list)
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-t <sec>, \-\-time <sec>
refresh rate in seconds (overrides \fB[global] refresh\fP) [default: 2 sec]
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-disable\-history
disable the stats history (same as \fB[global] history_size=0\fP)
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-stop\-after <n>
stop after n refreshes (TUI, stdout and \fB\-\-quiet\fP modes; under
\fB\-\-quiet\fP, n export cycles)
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-disable\-config\-exec
disable shell operator interpretation (\fB&&\fP, \fB|\fP, \fB>\fP) in the AMP and
on\-alert action commands read from \fBglances.conf\fP (recommended for system
services). The commands themselves still run: this is not a sandbox
.UNINDENT
.SS Server (REST API and Web UI)
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-server, \-w, \-\-webserver
run as a REST API server (FastAPI, \fB/api/5\fP) and serve the Web UI on
\fBbind_address:port\fP\&. Headless: no curses TUI. Without this flag, Glances
runs in TUI mode and does not bind any TCP socket. \fB\-w\fP/\fB\-\-webserver\fP
is the v4 spelling of the same mode (the v4 XML\-RPC server is gone)
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-B <addr>, \-\-bind <addr>
bind address (overrides \fB[outputs] bind_address\fP) [default: 127.0.0.1]
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-p <n>, \-\-port <n>
listening port (overrides \fB[outputs] port\fP) [default: 61208]. With
\fB\-\-client\fP: the server’s port
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-disable\-webui
serve the REST API without the Web UI (requires \fB\-\-server\fP)
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-api\-doc, \-\-no\-api\-doc
enable or disable the Swagger \fB/docs\fP and ReDoc \fB/redoc\fP pages
(overrides \fB[outputs] api_doc\fP)
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-enable\-mcp
mount the MCP (Model Context Protocol) endpoint (at \fB/mcp\fP, see
\fB\-\-mcp\-path\fP). Requires \fB\-\-server\fP and the \fBmcp\fP package, see
MCP (Model Context Protocol) server \%<#\:api-mcp>\&. Off by default
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-mcp\-path <path>
path the MCP endpoint is mounted at (overrides \fB[outputs] mcp_path\fP)
[default: /mcp]. Requires \fB\-\-server\fP
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-open\-web\-browser
open the Web UI in the default Web browser at startup (requires
\fB\-\-server\fP)
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-set\-password
generate a PBKDF2 password hash interactively and print it to stdout. Paste
it into \fB[outputs] password\fP of \fBglances.conf\fP to protect the server.
It does NOT modify \fBglances.conf\fP
.UNINDENT
.SS Client and browser
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-c <server>, \-\-client <server>
show a remote Glances v5 server in the TUI: \fBhost\fP, \fBhost:port\fP or an
\fBhttp(s)://\fP URL (default port: \fB\-\-port\fP, else 61208)
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-u <name>, \-\-username <name>
with \fB\-\-client\fP or \fB\-\-browser\fP: the server’s username [default: glances]
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-password
with \fB\-\-client\fP: prompt for the server’s password (else \fB[passwords]\fP
in \fBglances.conf\fP)
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-browser
browse the servers of \fB[serverlist]\fP in the TUI and open one as with
\fB\-\-client\fP\&. With \fB\-\-server\fP: serve that list on \fB/api/5/serverslist\fP
and on the \fB/browser\fP Web page
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-disable\-autodiscover
Zeroconf off: a server does not announce itself, a browser lists
\fB[serverlist]\fP only
.UNINDENT
.SS Exports
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-export <a,b>
enable export modules (comma\-separated list, e.g. \fBcsv,influxdb2\fP)
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-export\-csv\-file <path>
file path for the CSV exporter [default: ./glances.csv]
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-export\-csv\-overwrite
overwrite the CSV file instead of appending to it
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-export\-json\-file <path>
file path for the JSON exporter [default: ./glances.json]
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-export\-graph\-path <folder>
folder for the graph exporter’s SVG files [default: \fB[graph] path\fP,
else \fB~/.local/share/glances/graphs\fP]
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-export\-process\-filter EXPORT_PROCESS_FILTER
set the export process filter (comma\-separated list of regular expressions)
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet, \-\-no\-tui
disable the curses TUI (for example to only run the exports)
.UNINDENT
.SS Standard output and one\-shot modes
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-stdout <plugin[.key].attr,...>
print stats to stdout, one line per stat and refresh (e.g.
\fBcpu.user,mem.percent,network,all\fP). No TUI
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-stdout\-json <plugin,...>
print the selected plugins’ stats to stdout as one JSON object per
refresh. No TUI
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-stdout\-csv <plugin[.attr],...>
print the selected stats to stdout as CSV: a header line, then one line
per refresh. No TUI
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-fetch, \-\-stdout\-fetch
print a neofetch\-like summary of the machine, then exit (see Fetch \%<#\:fetch>)
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-fetch\-template <path>, \-\-stdout\-fetch\-template <path>
Jinja template for \fB\-\-fetch\fP (requires \fB\-\-fetch\fP)
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-api\-restful\-doc
print the REST API documentation (RST, real responses from this machine),
then exit
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-issue
test every plugin and print a Markdown report to paste into a bug report,
then exit
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-memory\-leak
test for memory leaks and exit: collect for \fB\-\-stop\-after\fP seconds
(default 60) to warm up, then as long again, and print the memory growth
between the two
.UNINDENT
.SS TUI display
.INDENT 0.0
