.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-b, \-\-byte
display network rate in bytes per second (default: bits per second)
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-diskio\-show\-ramfs
show RAM disks (\fBram*\fP) in the disk I/O plugin (hidden by default)
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-diskio\-iops
display disk I/O operations per second instead of byte rates
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-diskio\-latency
display disk I/O latency (ms per read/write operation) instead of byte
rates
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-fs\-free\-space
display filesystem free space instead of used space (config fallback:
\fB[fs] free_space\fP)
.UNINDENT
.SS Processes
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-sort\-processes {cpu_percent,memory_percent,username,cpu_times,io_counters,name,cpu_num}
sort processes by the given key
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-programs, \-\-program
accumulate processes by program
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-process\-short\-name
show the short process name in the command column (default)
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-process\-long\-name
show the full command line in the command column
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-hide\-kernel\-threads
hide kernel threads in the process list (not available on Windows)
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-f PROCESS_FILTER, \-\-process\-filter PROCESS_FILTER
set the process filter pattern (regular expression); TUI mode only
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-process\-focus PROCESS_FOCUS
set a process list to focus on (comma\-separated list of Glances
filters); TUI mode only (config fallback: \fB[processlist] focus\fP)
.UNINDENT
.SS Changes from Glances v4
.sp
Removed options: \fB\-P\fP/\fB\-\-plugins\fP (additional plugin directory),
\fB\-\-cached\-time\fP, \fB\-\-trace\-malloc\fP, \fB\-\-enable\-process\-extended\fP,
\fB\-\-disable\-check\-update\fP, \fB\-\-sparkline\fP, \fB\-\-theme\-white\fP (use
\fB[outputs] theme=light\fP) and the SNMP options (\fB\-\-snmp\-community\fP,
\fB\-\-snmp\-port\fP, \fB\-\-snmp\-version\fP, \fB\-\-snmp\-user\fP, \fB\-\-snmp\-auth\fP,
\fB\-\-snmp\-force\fP).
.sp
Changed options:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-s\fP/\fB\-\-server\fP is now the same mode as \fB\-w\fP/\fB\-\-webserver\fP (REST
API and Web UI); the XML\-RPC server and its port 61209 are gone, and
\fB\-c\fP/\fB\-\-client\fP talks to a Glances v5 REST server.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-B\fP/\fB\-\-bind\fP defaults to \fB127.0.0.1\fP (was \fB0.0.0.0\fP).
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-\-password\fP no longer defines a server password: use \fB\-\-set\-password\fP
and \fB[outputs] password\fP\&. It now only prompts for the server’s password
with \fB\-\-client\fP\&. \fB\-u\fP/\fB\-\-username\fP takes the name as a value and
only applies to \fB\-\-client\fP and \fB\-\-browser\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-\-api\-doc\fP toggles the Swagger and ReDoc pages of the server (it used
to print the Python API documentation).
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-\-fetch\-template\fP requires \fB\-\-fetch\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
.sp
The following commands (key pressed) are supported while in Glances
(press \fBh\fP to display them all):
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \fBF4\fP
Set the process filter
.sp
The filter is a regular expression pattern:
.INDENT 7.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBgnome\fP: matches all processes starting with the \fBgnome\fP
string
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\&.*gnome.*\fP: matches all processes containing the \fBgnome\fP
string
.UNINDENT
.TP
.B \fBENTER\fP
Show/hide the extended stats of the selected process
.TP
.B \fBa\fP
Sort process list automatically
.INDENT 7.0
.IP \(bu 2
If CPU \fB>70%\fP, sort processes by CPU usage
.IP \(bu 2
If MEM \fB>70%\fP, sort processes by MEM usage
.IP \(bu 2
If CPU iowait \fB>60%\fP, sort processes by I/O read and write
.UNINDENT
.TP
.B \fBA\fP
Show/hide the Application Monitoring Process (AMPs)
.TP
.B \fBb\fP
Switch between bit/s or Byte/s for network I/O
.TP
.B \fBB\fP
Switch between byte/s and I/O operations per second for disk I/O
.TP
.B \fBc\fP
Sort processes by CPU usage
.TP
.B \fBC\fP
Show/hide cloud stats
.TP
.B \fBd\fP
Show/hide disk I/O stats
.TP
.B \fBD\fP
Show/hide containers stats
.TP
.B \fBE\fP
Erase the current process filter
.TP
.B \fBf\fP
Show/hide file system and folder monitoring stats
.TP
.B \fBF\fP
Switch between file system used and free space
.TP
.B \fBg\fP
Generate graphs for current history (needs \fB\-\-export graph\fP)
.TP
.B \fBG\fP
Show/hide GPU stats
.TP
.B \fBh\fP
Show/hide the help screen (scroll it with \fBUP\fP/\fBDOWN\fP, \fBj\fP/\fBk\fP,
\fBPAGE\-UP\fP/\fBPAGE\-DOWN\fP and \fBHOME\fP)
.TP
.B \fBi\fP
Sort processes by I/O rate
.TP
.B \fBI\fP
Show/hide IP module
.TP
.B \fBj\fP
Switch between the processes (threads) and programs view
.TP
.B \fB+\fP
Increase selected process nice level / Lower the priority (need right) \- Not in client mode.
.TP
.B \fB\-\fP
Decrease selected process nice level / Higher the priority (need right) \- Not in client mode.
.TP
.B \fBk\fP
Kill selected process (need right, asks first) \- Not in client mode.
.TP
.B \fBK\fP
Show/hide TCP connections
.TP
.B \fBl\fP
Show/hide alerts
.TP
.B \fBL\fP
Switch between byte/s and latency for disk I/O
.TP
.B \fBm\fP
Sort processes by MEM usage
.TP
.B \fBM\fP
Reset the filtered processes summary min/max
.TP
.B \fBn\fP
Show/hide network stats
.TP
.B \fBN\fP
Show/hide current time
.TP
.B \fBo\fP
Sort processes by CPU core number
.TP
.B \fBp\fP
Sort processes by name
.TP
.B \fBP\fP
Show/hide ports stats
.TP
.B \fBq|ESC|CTRL\-C\fP
Quit the current Glances session
.TP
.B \fBQ\fP
Show/hide IRQ module
.TP
.B \fBr\fP
Show/hide SMART stats
.TP
.B \fBR\fP
Show/hide RAID plugin
.TP
.B \fBs\fP
Show/hide sensors plugin
.TP
.B \fBt\fP
Sort process by CPU times (TIME+)
.TP
.B \fBT\fP
View network and disk I/O as a combination
.TP
.B \fBu\fP
Sort processes by USER
.TP
.B \fBU\fP
View cumulative network and disk I/O
.TP
.B \fBV\fP
Show/hide VMS plugin
.TP
.B \fBW\fP
Show/hide Wifi module
.TP
.B \fBz\fP
Show/hide processes stats
.TP
.B \fB0\fP
Enable/disable Irix/Solaris mode
.sp
The load and the task’s CPU usage will be divided by the total number of CPUs
.TP
.B \fB1\fP
Switch between global CPU and per\-CPU stats
.TP
.B \fB2\fP
Show/hide the left sidebar
.TP
.B \fB3\fP
Show/hide the quick look module
.TP
.B \fB4\fP
Enable/disable the full\-width quick look
.TP
.B \fB5\fP
Show/hide the top menu (QuickLook, CPU, MEM, SWAP, and LOAD)
.TP
.B \fB6\fP
Enable/disable mean GPU mode
